This project builds technique knowledge on the open-source projects listed
below. Each entry gives the source URL, its license, the full license text
carried in this repository, the upstream commit the pack was built against,
whether the content was modified, and how it was derived. Entries are added
as upstream packs are vendored.

Vendored upstream content:

Each entry below follows the format shown here. Append one block per vendored
pack, in the same shape, separated by a blank line. The indented block is a
template, not an entry; the "#" prefix marks it as such.

    # Pack:         <registry pack id, matching registry/packs/<id>/pack.yaml>
    # Source:       <upstream repository URL>
    # License:      <SPDX identifier, as read from the upstream LICENSE file>
    # Copyright:    <copyright holder, as named in that LICENSE file>
    # License-Text: <path in this repository to the verbatim upstream license>
    # Upstream-Notice: <path to the verbatim upstream NOTICE, or "none in upstream">
    # Commit:       <full upstream commit SHA the pack was built against>
    # Modified:     <yes | no — whether upstream content is reproduced altered>
    # Derivation:   <copied | inspired — see the note below>

Derivation values. "copied" means upstream text is reproduced in this
repository, verbatim or modified; the license's conditions on redistribution
apply, and for Apache-2.0 the statement of changes required by section 4(b)
belongs on the "Modified" line and in the pack's own entries. "inspired" means
no upstream text is reproduced: the entries are written for this registry and
the upstream is credited as the source of the subject matter and as the reason
the pack exists. Both are recorded here, because an "inspired" pack still
names the upstream and still pins the commit it was built against.

